Write a Python function:

    def parse_csv_line(line: str) -> list[str]

It splits a single CSV line into its fields. Rules:
- The delimiter is the comma.
- Fields may be enclosed in double quotes.
- Inside a quoted field, a comma is treated as a regular character.
- Inside a quoted field, "" represents a single double-quote character.
- Empty fields produce an empty string.
- Whitespace outside of quotes is preserved as-is.

Do NOT use the csv module or any other library.

Afterwards: write 6 assert statements that test your function,
including at least two cases with escaped quotes.

